# Read-only interface and address report.
# JSON keeps the external output machine-readable; yesh does not parse or
# rewrite it. Permission errors remain errors and no fallback is attempted.
#
# Bash comparison:
#   ip -j address show
# The yesh form makes the exact read-only argv visible in --plan.

# Role of yesh: make the read-only network check and failure path explicit; Linux networking tools provide the observation.
ip -j address show
